⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
283 calories 37g protein (for the entire pint, toppings/mix-ins included)

Phish Food Protein Ice Cream 😋🍦

Full recipe book (170+ flavors) in bio!

- 1 Chocolate Protein Shake (350-400ml)  
- 25g sweetener
- 10g cocoa powder
- A pinch of salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins:
- 10g mini lucky-charms-style marshmallows (I used the ones from Jet Puffed)
- 7g caramel syrup
- ½ of a Hormbles Chormbles (protein chocolate bar with 100 cal and 10g pro)
—or—
Use the chocolate chip hack: 
- Right before the Mix-In cycle, combine 15g of chocolate with 2g of coconut oil, melt in the microwave (30 sec intervals, stirring in between), hollow out a hole in the center of the base, and pour in. After spinning on the Mix-In setting, it’ll turn into perfect, creamy chocolate chips. 
283 cal 24g C, 7g F, 37g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
3. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
4. Spin on “Respin” setting
5. Respin again if powdery
6. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with ¾ of the chocolate and marshmallows 
7. Run the “Mix-in” cycle
8. Top with the caramel syrup and the rest of the chocolate and marshmallows

